  "idea": "A **comparison sort** is an algorithm that sorts an array of comparable elements by determining their relative order through pairwise comparisons. The algorithm reads the input array, performs comparisons between elements using a total ordering relation (typically $\\leq$ or $<$), and produces a sorted permutation of the input.\n\nIn the context of parallel computing, a comparison sort refers specifically to algorithms designed to exploit parallelism—most notably **parallel merge sort**—which decompose the sorting problem into independent subproblems that can be solved concurrently.",
