  "idea": "A **fractional cut** is a relaxation of the classical integral multicut problem in graph theory. For a directed graph $G = (V, E)$ with a set of demand pairs $P \\subseteq V \\times V$, a fractional cut assigns non-negative real weights $w_e \\in [0, 1]$ to each edge $e \\in E$ such that for every demand pair $(s_i, t_i) \\in P$, the total weight along any path from $s_i$ to $t_i$ is at least 1.\n\nFormally, a fractional cut must satisfy:\n$$\\sum_{e \\in \\text{path}(s_i, t_i)} w_e \\geq 1 \\quad \\forall (s_i, t_i) \\in P$$\n\nThe **cost** or **weight** of a fractional cut is:\n$$\\text{FCut}(G, P) = \\min \\sum_{e \\in E} c_e \\cdot w_e$$\n\nwhere $c_e$ denotes the capacity of edge $e$.",
