  "idea": "A **fundamental cycle** is a cycle formed in an undirected graph by adding a single non-tree edge to a spanning tree. Formally, given a spanning tree $T$ of graph $G$ and a non-tree edge $e = (u, v) \\notin T$, the fundamental cycle is the unique cycle formed by $e$ together with the unique path between $u$ and $v$ in $T$:\n\n$$C_e = P_T(u,v) \\cup \\{e\\}$$\n\nwhere $P_T(u,v)$ denotes the unique tree path connecting vertices $u$ and $v$ in $T$.\n\nEach non-tree edge generates exactly one fundamental cycle, and the set of all fundamental cycles forms a **fundamental cycle basis** for the graph.",
